+over F_p, to have {degree} distinct nonzero roots, and to have zero coefficient
+at z^{degree - 1}.  A missing exponent below means coefficient zero.  Polynomial
+term order has no meaning; coefficients are canonical residues 0 through p-1.
+
+Source code C(S), encoded by D_S:
+{_format_terms(inst['source_terms'])}
+
+Target code C(T), encoded by D_T:
+{_format_terms(inst['target_terms'])}
+
+Find integers a,b in the inclusive range 1 through {modulus - 1} such that
+b is the multiplicative inverse of a modulo p and T={{a*s mod p : s in S}}.
+Equivalently, the exact coefficient identity is
