+
+# p is the cyclic-code length.  q is a prime with q == 1 (mod p), so every
+# q-cyclotomic class modulo p is a singleton and every exponent subset defines
+# a cyclic code over F_q.  n is a lower bound on the number of defining zeros;
+# make_instance advances it to the first degree coprime to p-1 so the answer is
+# unique.  The answer itself remains two integers as the haystack grows.
+DIFFICULTY: dict = {
