+NOTES: str = r"""
+Definition and reduction.  Section II defines permutation equivalence by
+sigma(C) and the affine maps tau_{a,b}; Section III defines the multiplier
+M_a=tau_{a,0}.  Its opening criterion says that when gcd(n,phi(n))=1, two
+cyclic codes are permutation-equivalent exactly when a multiplier does it.
+For prime length p this hypothesis always holds.  A defining set S records
+the exponents s for which zeta^s is a zero of the code.  Because the chosen
+prime field size q satisfies q=1 mod p, all q-cyclotomic classes are singleton,
+so an arbitrary S is a legitimate exact code description.  D_S(z)=prod(z-s)
+is merely a lossless polynomial packaging of that native defining set.
+
+Step-0 algorithm check.  This paper supplies structural classifications and an
+explicitly restricted equivalence search, not average-case hardness.  Track A
+would therefore be false here.  The Section III mechanical route enumerates
+the p-1 multipliers; on this distribution its fastest filter tests the constant
+coefficient, costing O(p log k+k) exact modular operations.  The compact Track B
