+ratio has one kth root, recovered by one modular exponentiation.  selftest
+measures both routes at the shipping preset rather than hiding the algorithm.
+
+Certificate construction.  The source defining set is sampled first, uniformly
+subject to having k distinct nonzero exponents and sum zero.  The zero sum makes
+the tempting linear coefficient ratio uninformative.  A nontrivial multiplier
+a is then sampled and the target set aS is formed.  Both displayed polynomials
+are expanded from those held roots, while the witness (a,a^{-1}) is already
+known.  This is a transformation of a known instance, never a solve.
+
+Easy cases avoided.  Section II calls the zero, whole-space, repetition, and
+dual-repetition codes elementary; a proper defining set of size between 7 and
+p-2 avoids them.  Remark 2's length-p-over-F_p MDS situation is also avoided:
+the code alphabet is F_q with q>p and q=1 mod p.  The first coefficient below
+the leading term is forced to zero so direct linear-ratio, magnitude-outlier,
+and greedy first-coefficient heuristics do not reveal the plant.  Random
+restart samples the full structurally valid multiplier language.  The fourth
+attack treats the constant-term ratio as if its weight were one; it is a
+plausible by-hand ansatz and fails because the actual weight is k.
+""".strip()
