 ## Caveats
 
-- This is a Track B insight benchmark, not a claim that cyclic-code equivalence
-  or this planted distribution is computationally hard.  The disclosed compact
-  algorithm solves every generated instance efficiently once the invariant is
-  known.
-- `D_S` is a lossless defining-set polynomial, not the usual generator
-  polynomial over `F_q`.  The code-equivalence-to-multiplier reduction is the
-  paper's; the polynomial packaging is an exact representation chosen by this
-  benchmark.
-- The `0/200,000` figure uses the declared prior: uniform `a in F_p^*`, with
-  `a^-1` filled in for free.  It is an observed density, not a confidence-bound
-  proof.  Uniqueness is proved separately by `gcd(k,p-1)=1` and the nonzero
-  constant coefficient.
-- Polynomial factorization over `F_p`, generic code-equivalence software, and
-  a CAS implementation of weighted coefficient matching were not run as
-  failing attacks.  They are efficient tool-based alternatives and belong on
-  the Track B reference side, not among attacks expected to fail without tools.
-- The zero-sum condition deliberately kills the immediately linear `z^(k-1)`
-  ratio.  A solver that recognizes any other nonzero coefficient's weight can
-  also recover a short list of candidates; this is another expression of the
-  intended invariant, not independent hardness.
-- Most importantly, the four-vendor bare/hinted/placebo experiments are
-  pending because the configured OpenRouter key is over its total limit.  Do
-  not interpret the error-only transcript as evidence that any model failed.
+- This is deliberately not a complexity-theoretic hardness claim. Exact software
+  solves the hard preset in a fraction of a millisecond; the benchmark tests
+  recognition and execution of a no-tool compression.
+- The exact density uses the proof that a t-element subset of the quotient cannot
+  have a nontrivial translation stabilizer when `gcd(t,(p-1)/m)=1`. The sampled
+  0/200,000 figure measures a uniform nonzero multiplier with its inverse already
+  filled in; it does not measure resistance to algebraic analysis.
+- Generation conditions on the listed cheap signatures failing. This prevents a
+  known planting leak but means the instance distribution is not an unconditional
+  random distribution of orbit representatives.
+- The quotient-product invariant itself solves every generated instance. That is
+  the intended Track B route, not an omitted attack. No support-splitting package,
+  general code-equivalence canonicalizer, or CAS was run; each would be expected
+  to succeed and would not strengthen this no-tool claim.
+- The quasi-cyclic conjectural results in Section IV are not used. This family uses
+  only the exact cyclic-code definitions and multiplier action from Sections II–III.
+- Prime testing is deterministic over the 64-bit range containing all presets and
+  tested escalations. Extremely large user-supplied `n` outside that range is not
+  supported by the stated primality guarantee.
+- Most importantly, the four-vendor oracle and both G9 comparison arms remain
+  unmeasured because the configured OpenRouter key has no remaining limit.
