 | 4 | unmeasured |\n| placebo hint | 0 / 0 | 4 | unmeasured |\n\n`hinted - placebo` is undefined; the schema stores `0.0` only as a placeholder.\nThe hint names the quotient-product invariant without giving an algorithmic chain.\nNo claim about hint responsiveness is possible until valid oracle calls run.\n\n## Use\n\n```python\nimport gen_1002_2456 as g\n\ninst = g.make_instance(seed=17, **g.DIFFICULTY[\"hard\"])\nstatement = g.render(inst)\ncandidate = g.parse_answer(\n    \"<answer>\" + __import__(\"json\").dumps(inst[\"answer\"]) + \"</answer>\"\n)\nassert g.verify(inst, candidate) == (True, \"ok\")\n```\n\nAfter OpenRouter capacity is restored, rerun\n`python3 ../../scripts/harden.py gen_1002_2456.py` here, then rerun the hinted and\nplacebo copies in separate directories. From the repository root, emission is\n`bash scripts/emit.sh 1002.2456` after a genuine `hardened` verdict exists.\n\n## Caveats\n\n- This is deliberately not a complexity-theoretic hardness claim. Exact software\n  solves the hard preset in a fraction of a millisecond; the benchmark tests\n  recognition and execution of a no-tool compression.\n- The exact density uses the proof that a t-element subset of the quotient cannot\n  have a nontrivial translation stabilizer when `gcd(t,(p-1)/m)=1`. The sampled\n  0/200,000 figure measures a uniform nonzero multiplier with its inverse already\n  filled in; it does not measure resistance to algebraic analysis.\n- Generation conditions on the listed cheap signatures failing. This prevents a\n  known planting leak but means the instance distribution is not an unconditional\n  random distribution of orbit representatives.\n- The quotient-product invariant itself solves every generated instance. That is\n  the intended Track B route, not an omitted attack. No support-splitting package,\n  general code-equivalence canonicalizer, or CAS was run; each would be expected\n  to succeed and would not strengthen this no-tool claim.\n- The quasi-cyclic conjectural results in Section IV are not used. This family uses\n  only the exact cyclic-code definitions and multiplier action from Sections II–III.\n- Prime testing is deterministic over the 64-bit range containing all presets and\n  tested escalations. Extremely large user-supplied `n` outside that range is not\n  supported by the stated primality guarantee.\n- Most importantly, the four-vendor oracle and both G9 comparison arms remain\n  unmeasured because the configured OpenRouter key has no remaining limit.\nTrue\n{\n  \"demo_bruteforce_valid_solution_count\": 4,\n  \"pass\": true,\n  \"shipping_exact_solution_fraction\": 7.999996160001843e-08,\n  \"shipping_exact_valid_solution_count\": 8,\n  \"shipping_sampled_solution_fraction\": 0.0,\n  \"shipping_sampled_solution_hits\": 0,\n  \"shipping_sampled_solution_total\": 200000,\n  \"strongest_attack_mean_operations\": 975.875,\n  \"strongest_attack_operations\": 7807,\n  \"strongest_attack_solved_instances\": 8,\n  \"strongest_attack_wall_sec\": 0.001071\n}\n{\n  \"answer_chars\": 19,\n  \"answer_elements\": 2,\n  \"answer_tokens\": 5,\n  \"arms\": {\n    \"bare\": {\n      \"attempts\": 0,\n      \"solved\": 0\n    },\n    \"hinted\": {\n      \"attempts\": 0,\n      \"solved\": 0\n    },\n    \"placebo\": {\n      \"attempts\": 0,\n      \"solved\": 0\n    }\n  },\n  \"caps\": {\n    \"chars\": 2000,\n    \"elements\": 256,\n    \"operations\": 300\n  },\n  \"compact_route_verified\": \"8/8\",\n  \"hinted_minus_placebo\": 0.0,\n  \"hinted_verdict\": \"unmeasured\",\n  \"intended_route_operations\": 98,\n  \"pass\": true\n}\n{\n \"paper\": \"1002.2456\",\n \"schema_version\": 2,\n \"model\": \"gpt-5.6-sol\",\n \"effort\": \"xhigh\",\n \"codex_version\": \"0.150.1\",\n \"started_at\": \"2026-09-05T05:37:22Z\",\n \"harden_master_seed\": 7269817860010737882,\n \"oracle_pool\": [\n  \"openai/gpt-5.6-terra\",\n  \"anthropic/claude-sonnet-5\",\n  \"google/gemini-3.1-pro-preview\",\n  \"x-ai/grok-4.6\"\n ],\n \"oracle_effort\