codex
The stronger audit changes the Track B evidence materially: the fastest straightforward exact scan is not the million-operation orbit expansion previously reported. Precomputing quotient-coset labels reduces it to an average of about 5,694 modular operations (8/8 successes, roughly 0.4 ms locally). That is still far beyond a no-tool hand execution, while the product invariant stays under the 300-operation cap, so Track B remains defensible; I’ve corrected the module to report the stronger algorithm and the natural `integer_tuple` certificate type.
