codex
Completed a verified Track B generator based on the paper’s cyclic-code multiplier equivalence framework ([arXiv paper](https://arxiv.org/pdf/1002.2456)).

Deliverables:

- [gen_1002_2456.py](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.2456/gen_1002_2456.py)
- [selftest_report.json](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.2456/selftest_report.json)
- [README.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.2456/README.md)
- [llm_loop_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.2456/llm_loop_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.2456/g9_hinted_transcript.jsonl)
- [g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1002.2456/g9_placebo_transcript.jsonl)

Results:

- All G1–G9 gates pass.
- Shipping preset: `easy`.
- Guess probability: \(16/20{,}000{,}030 \approx 8.0\times10^{-7}\).
- Reference algorithm: 874.125 mean exact operations, succeeds 8/8 as expected.
- Compact route: at most 144 operations.
- Oracle arms: bare 0/3, hinted 0/3, placebo 0/3.
- Additional fuzz audit passed on 400 deterministic instances.

The README explicitly records that the current repository harness used its configured two-vendor pool, rather than the four-vendor pool described in the task text.
